==Trivia==
* Despite sharing nomenclature, Wasteland Coyotes share few behavioral characteristics with true {{Wp|coyote}}s, which are generally smaller canines that rarely function together as packs. Reports on coyotes attacking humans are rare, and though hardy animals, they are not specifically adapted for the desert.

==Nomenclature==
The Japanese name for Wasteland Coyotes, ''Karakara Koyōte'' (カラカラコヨーテ), refers to the onomatopoeia ''karakara'' meaning "dry".
